# Keep the build context small, and keep local state out of images.
#
# A note on patterns: Docker matches these against the FULL path and `*` does
# not cross a `/`. So `*.db` matches only top-level files, which is why every
# data pattern below is also spelled with `**/`. Without that, backups/*.db --
# real financial records -- would be sent to the daemon and land in the build
# stage via `COPY . .`. The multi-stage build keeps them out of the published
# image, but they have no business in the context or the builder cache either.

.git/
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
compose.yaml
compose.prod.yaml

# Local secrets must never reach an image layer or the build context.
.env
.env.local
*.env
!*.env.example

# Local data. The database and every snapshot of it.
data/
backups/
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.partial

# Build output
bin/
dist/
*.exe

# Local scratch that Git ignores and Docker otherwise would not: prompt
# transcripts, screenshots, working notes. They are untracked, so what is in the
# context differs from one machine to the next -- which is exactly what stops a
# build being reproducible. Top-level only, deliberately: `*` does not cross a
# `/`, and there is nothing under web/ this could reach.
*.txt
*.png

# Not needed to compile: documentation and the server-side deployment files,
# which are read on the host rather than inside the image.
README.md
CLAUDE.md
docs/
deploy/

# Editors / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
